    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "**Fight Club** (1999) revolutionized psychological thrillers by merging brutal nihilism with razor-sharp satire of consumer culture. Director David Fincher crafted a visual masterpiece that influenced countless films, from **Inception** (2010) to **Mr. Robot** (2015-2019). The film's innovative narrative techniques, including unreliable narration and subliminal frame splicing, created a new template for mind-bending storytelling. Like **American Psycho** (2000), it savagely critiques masculine identity and corporate conformity while maintaining a darkly comic edge."
      },
      {
        "type": "movies",
