      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's influence extends deep into modern psychological thrillers. **Shutter Island** (2010) and **Black Swan** (2010) borrowed Fight Club's unreliable narrator technique to explore fractured identities. The theme of anti-consumerism and systemic rebellion echoes through films like **V for Vendetta** (2005) and **Sorry to Bother You** (2018), though none match Fight Club's raw anarchic energy."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Fight Club's visual style defined modern psychological thrillers. Fincher's green-yellow color palette and kinetic camera work influenced films like **Requiem for a Dream** (2000) and **Donnie Darko** (2001). The film's mix of violence and philosophy created a template for intelligent action films like **The Matrix** (1999) and **Drive** (2011). SUBHEAD: Modern Identity Crisis Films"
      },
      {
        "type": "movies",
        "movies": [
          {
            "title": "Mulholland Drive",
            "year": 2001,
            "slug": "David Lynch's surreal masterpiece about identity and Hollywood dreams.",
            "poster": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/x7A59t6ySylr1L7aubOQEA480vM.jpg",
            "initialStreaming": "HBO Max",
            "tmdb_id": 1018,
            "poster_url": "https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w500/x7A59t6ySylr1L7aubOQEA480vM.jpg"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Contemporary filmmakers continue drawing from Fight Club's exploration of masculine identity crisis. **The Master** (2012) and **Joker** (2019) examine similar themes of alienation and societal disconnect. **Nightcrawler** (2014) updates Fight Club's critique of capitalism for the digital age, while maintaining its dark satirical edge."
      }
